  "intro": "The binomial series generalizes the binomial theorem to any real power $k$: for $|x|<1$, $(1+x)^k=\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty\\binom{k}{n}x^n$, where $\\binom{k}{n}=\\frac{k(k-1)\\cdots(k-n+1)}{n!}$. When $k$ is a positive integer it terminates (the ordinary expansion); otherwise it is an infinite series. It is useful for approximating roots and for building new series by substitution, and for integrating functions with no elementary antiderivative term by term.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Write the first three terms of the binomial series for $(1+x)^{1/2}$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Here $k=\\frac{1}{2}$. Compute coefficients: $\\binom{1/2}{0}=1$, $\\binom{1/2}{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$.",
          "$\\binom{1/2}{2}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-1\\right)}{2!}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot(-\\frac{1}{2})}{2}=-\\frac{1}{8}$.",
          "So $(1+x)^{1/2}=1+\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{8}x^2+\\cdots$."
        ],
        "answer": "$1+\\dfrac{1}{2}x-\\dfrac{1}{8}x^2+\\cdots$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Use the binomial series to approximate $\\sqrt{1.04}$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Write $\\sqrt{1.04}=(1+0.04)^{1/2}$ and use the first two terms $1+\\frac{1}{2}x$.",
          "Substitute $x=0.04$: $1+\\frac{1}{2}(0.04)=1+0.02=1.02$.",
          "So $\\sqrt{1.04}\\approx 1.02$ (exact $\\approx 1.0198$)."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\sqrt{1.04}\\approx 1.02$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Expand $(1+x)^{-1}$ with the binomial series and compare to the geometric series.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "With $k=-1$: $\\binom{-1}{n}=(-1)^n$, so $(1+x)^{-1}=\\sum(-1)^n x^n$.",
          "This is $1-x+x^2-x^3+\\cdots$.",
          "It matches the geometric series for $\\frac{1}{1+x}$, valid for $|x|<1$."
        ],
        "answer": "$(1+x)^{-1}=\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty(-1)^n x^n$"
      }
    },
    {
